1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,700
After discharge, readings alone are not enough. WardZero connects a synthetic home-care patient,

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,207
explained concern, and a caregiver who takes responsibility.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,319
These readings travel from the browser simulator through a validated API into embedded

4
00:00:17,319 --> 00:00:22,637
PostgreSQL. Three recent stable observations establish Low concern. Measurement time and arrival time

5
00:00:22,637 --> 00:00:27,956
are preserved. Missing or stale evidence is shown explicitly rather than labeled safe.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,339
Now the caregiver records: more tired today and barely ate lunch. This is

7
00:00:38,339 --> 00:00:43,679
a live Gemini request. The adapter accepts only allowed observations and literal source

8
00:00:43,679 --> 00:00:49,018
excerpts, including negation and time context. These current observations raise Low concern to

9
00:00:49,018 --> 00:00:54,358
Medium. A deterioration preset then sends additional readings through normal ingestion, raising concern

10
00:00:54,358 --> 00:00:58,054
to High. Every explanation points back to stored evidence.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,155
One active episode belongs to the assigned caregiver. Acknowledgement takes ownership, but does

12
00:01:10,155 --> 00:01:15,310
not resolve it. The caregiver records an action, then a separate resolution reason.

13
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:20,466
Actor, time, and each transition remain in the audit trail. Closing the response

14
00:01:20,466 --> 00:01:25,621
does not rewrite the patient's current concern. These actions describe a synthetic review;

15
00:01:25,621 --> 00:01:28,000
the app does not prescribe treatment.

16
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,528
In a separate run, sensor transport goes offline while the dashboard remains connected.

17
00:01:44,528 --> 00:01:50,056
Three readings are saved in IndexedDB before transmission. The visibly accelerated clock makes

18
00:01:50,056 --> 00:01:55,583
monitoring delayed, then offline. Refresh preserves the pending queue. Reconnection drains it into

19
00:01:55,583 --> 00:02:01,111
the database once, with original observation times. Old readings do not pretend to

20
00:02:01,111 --> 00:02:06,639
be fresh. Lost acknowledgements and duplicate retries are also covered by executable tests.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,003
This new run leaves a High-concern alert unanswered. Advancing the labeled demo clock

22
00:02:20,003 --> 00:02:25,005
crosses the acknowledgement deadline. The alert appears in the backup coordinator's inbox, where

23
00:02:25,005 --> 00:02:30,008
Ravi can respond. This is in-app escalation, not a text message or phone

24
00:02:30,008 --> 00:02:35,011
call. A separate production-server test verifies that the deadline worker also runs with

25
00:02:35,011 --> 00:02:36,550
every browser page closed.

26
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:48,073
The repository includes forty-seven automated tests, eight browser journeys, live Gemini evidence, and

27
00:02:48,073 --> 00:02:53,146
reproducible setup. This is a local prototype using synthetic data and engineering rules,

28
00:02:53,146 --> 00:02:58,220
with no clinical validation or forty-eight-hour prediction claim. WardZero makes the handoff visible

29
00:02:58,220 --> 00:02:59,000
and accountable.
